WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:06.283
Hey builders So today I'm going to talk
to you about Base hard forks So Base

00:00:06.283 --> 00:00:08.900
hard forks change how the chain works

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:14.307
So what I'm going to go through today is
how can you know what changes impact your

00:00:14.307 --> 00:00:17.600
app and how early can you find
out how early can you test

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:24.280
So I want to introduce you guys to Vibenet
You've probably heard us talk about

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:29.116
Vibenet tweet about Vibenet but what is
Vibenet So Vibenet is Base's experimental

00:00:29.116 --> 00:00:34.324
preview network That means that new hard
fork features go live here first often

00:00:34.324 --> 00:00:39.160
weeks before they even reach Sepolia or
Mainnet For example we're getting ready

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:43.624
for 200 millisecond blocks that are
already running on Vibenet today while

00:00:43.624 --> 00:00:46.600
Sepolia is actually planned
for later in October

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:55.750
So what should you test Well you can
start with your own app and point it

00:00:55.750 --> 00:01:00.138
at Vibenet and run your normal flows
deploy your contracts any transactions

00:01:00.138 --> 00:01:01.600
check indexers frontends etc

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:07.729
Look for anything that behaves differently
look for timing assumptions RPC responses

00:01:07.729 --> 00:01:13.479
gaps or even events Then try the new
features themselves and ask yourself how

00:01:13.479 --> 00:01:18.300
does it testing on Vibenet is really easy
with AI you just need to add the skills

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:24.444
work So I'm going to put that link in
the comments below And that's already

00:01:24.444 --> 00:01:30.288
live and you can get started So your
agents will have everything you need to

00:01:30.288 --> 00:01:35.352
test anything on Vibenet Another thing is
going to chain.base.org We actually have

00:01:35.352 --> 00:01:37.300
all the demos here for

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:44.029
everything that will be going to Vibenet
or new features So for example if you're

00:01:44.029 --> 00:01:49.283
wanting to learn about EIP-8130 how that's
going to affect user experiences how you

00:01:49.283 --> 00:01:54.912
can implement feel free to click on
accounts If you are working with B20 and

00:01:54.912 --> 00:02:00.542
you want to know what is the next
features for B20 you can always check

00:02:00.542 --> 00:02:06.171
out the demos here You can even deploy
test tokens for B20 directly on Vibenet

00:02:06.171 --> 00:02:11.800
And we also have a validity transactions
as well which is going live on Cobalt

00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:22.940
And if you hit something unexpected you
can tell us in our Base Discord Include

00:02:22.940 --> 00:02:25.900
your transaction hash what you
expected and the exact error

00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:32.131
Vibenet is our ground zero for what's next
on Base So test early tell us what breaks

00:02:32.131 --> 00:02:34.900
and be ready for day one Thanks guys Bye
